    "fN": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "page": "flows",
      "text": "How to view it\n\n• Play button on each screen: buttons and tabs work.\n• Animations respect the system “reduce motion” setting.\n• Desktop only: there is no phone version (decided).",
      "w": 420,
      "x": 8160,
      "y": 0
    },
    "sDec": {
      "fill": "green",
      "page": "v03",
      "text": "Decisions these screens reflect\n\n• A desk of N machines (2 today), each by its id and name. No fixed “Mac/PC” in the code: the icon comes from the detected OS.\n• Side navigation: Desk · Tunnels · Monitors · Network · Arrangement, plus one page per machine.\n• Each machine announces modules with a state and a reason (nothing is hidden without explanation).\n• Tunnels: Claude opens a tunnel from one machine to another and does anything inside (commands, processes, files, ports). It survives the link.\n• Monitors with a single standard: one owner per monitor, input confirmed by the firmware and “unsupported” visible.\n• Scenes instead of fixed modes.\n• All configuration from the UI.\n• Keyboard and mouse with no owner: they work from any machine and Tandem follows the one you use.\n• Tunnels are read-only in the UI: Claude manages them over MCP; the app shows them.\n• Buttons: a single system (fixed height, icon always, glow, elevation and focus). Screens at real scale.",
      "w": 440,
      "x": 5440,
      "y": 0
    },
    "sHoy": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "page": "today",
      "text": "What is shown today\n\n• Two fixed cards: “Mac” on the left, “PC” on the right.\n• Monitors and modes greyed out (“coming soon”), since T-092.\n• Services (SSH, folders, RTX 5080, files) locked: “requires cable”.\n• 4-step setup designed for exactly two machines.\n\nUnderlying problem: the structure assumes two machines and one OS per side. There is no room for compute, resources or a third machine.",
      "w": 420,
      "x": 4540,
      "y": 0
    },
    "sQ": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "v03",
      "text": "Questions for later\n\n1. Trust with N machines: does a new machine join with a single code and the others accept it, or is each pair paired?\n3. Configuration conflicts: does the most recent version win per section, or is the user asked?\n4. Missing modules: are they shown off with their reason (as drawn) or hidden?\n5. Side navigation (proposed) or a single live scene as today, with panels?\n6. Accent per machine: do you pick it or is it assigned automatically?\n8. ⌘K palette: does it also launch jobs written in natural language for Claude, or only Tandem commands?",
      "w": 440,
      "x": 5440,
      "y": 700
    },
